  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Let me summarize what was done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI rewrote `mergeRanges(ranges)` in `ranges.mjs`. The original implementation had four bugs: it mutated the input array and pairs, performed no validation, didn't merge adjacent integers, and let contained intervals shorten the current interval.\n\n### Changes made\n\n**Validation (throws `TypeError`):**\n- Non-array input\n- Elements that aren't 2-element arrays\n- Bounds that aren't safe integers (`Number.isSafeInteger`)\n- `start > end`\n\n**Correct merging:**\n- Copies each pair into a fresh `[start, end]` array, so the input array and its pairs are never mutated.\n- Sorts by start, then end (`a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]`).\n- Merges when `start <= last[1] + 1`, which handles both overlap and adjacency (`[2,4]` + `[5,7]` → `[2,7]`).\n- Only extends the current interval when `end > last[1]`, so contained intervals can't shorten it.\n- Returns fresh pair arrays inside a fresh result array; empty input returns `[]`.\n\n### Verification against the provided tests\n- `mergeRanges([[8,10],[1,3],[2,5]])` → `[[1,5],[8,10]]` ✓\n- `mergeRanges([[5,7],[2,4]])` → `[[2,7]]` ✓ (adjacency)\n\nThe named export `mergeRanges` is preserved.",
